insert into "il_translations" ("lesson_id", "lang", "key", "text") select "lesson_id", "lang", "key", "text" from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::"il_translations", $sync$[{"key":"title","lang":"en-US","text":"What does a last letter ask someone to do?","lesson_id":"3fb72aa8-9f92-408e-b1c6-b26b71312916"},{"key":"intro","lang":"en-US","text":"Some things people only manage to write down. This is the end of a letter from the film Me Before You.","lesson_id":"3fb72aa8-9f92-408e-b1c6-b26b71312916"},{"key":"explore","lang":"en-US","text":"## The film\r\nMe Before You (2016) is based on the novel by Jojo Moyes. Emilia Clarke plays Louisa Clark, a cheerful young woman hired to care for Will Traynor, who was paralysed after an accident. Sam Claflin plays Will.\r\n\r\n## The letter\r\nAfter Will dies, Louisa reads the letter he left for her at a cafe in Paris, as he asked. He mentions the money that will help her start again and hopes she will live more boldly.\r\n\r\n## Lines worth keeping\r\n- \"Wear those stripy legs with pride\": be proud of who you are, striped tights and all.\r\n- \"You are scored on my heart\": you are carved into my heart.\r\n- \"Just live well\": simply live a good life.\r\n\r\nThe video places this letter after a song, so the practice uses only the spoken part, where the voice is clear and slow.","lesson_id":"3fb72aa8-9f92-408e-b1c6-b26b71312916"},{"key":"title","lang":"en-US","text":"Can confidence be trained like a muscle?","lesson_id":"bfd37ff0-5b16-4600-81ce-3fada909932d"},{"key":"intro","lang":"en-US","text":"Some think talent is fixed, others think it grows. That belief changes more than you expect.","lesson_id":"bfd37ff0-5b16-4600-81ce-3fada909932d"},{"key":"explore","lang":"en-US","text":"## Where confidence comes from\r\nThis TED-Ed video names three sources: what you are born with, how others treat you, and your own choices. The last one is yours to control.\r\n\r\n## Three tips\r\n- A quick fix: picture success, strike a powerful pose, give yourself a pep talk.\r\n- Believe you can improve.\r\n- Practise failing.\r\n\r\n## Two mindsets\r\nA fixed mindset treats talent as locked in. A growth mindset treats a challenge as a chance to learn.","lesson_id":"bfd37ff0-5b16-4600-81ce-3fada909932d"},{"key":"vocab:9ef47591-450d-44ad-b049-4b78e8e98703","lang":"en-US","text":"at any moment","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:75f688ed-7c98-46b0-b45d-cfedda861415","lang":"en-US","text":"a terrible disaster","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:18853913-606c-471d-9a3f-53a4bf865e59","lang":"en-US","text":"people you know a little","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:89f9c702-a521-4902-ba53-21ee80362693","lang":"en-US","text":"slightly","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:57d1ce1c-8e97-443b-af51-835d9f0584cf","lang":"en-US","text":"to finish with a particular result","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:49f4c426-6950-4a52-acc0-7ced69585ccb","lang":"en-US","text":"asks to what degree we need to do something","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:5ad9511d-e759-473b-b193-f3fb82047803","lang":"en-US","text":"to hold on tightly","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:43cd54ea-7dd3-43b3-9963-4d39d1a72a2f","lang":"en-US","text":"to leave something behind","lesson_id":"a9f2f481-b123-4144-b020-cbe8b79f1aaa"},{"key":"vocab:e9af59a4-e4a1-4282-9483-af7b8fd4a0fa","lang":"en-US","text":"people you share a house with","lesson_id":"8697a61b-9d6d-4265-98c1-565fe58f539e"},{"key":"vocab:104e6e7e-d9a4-4460-9902-ce174373c5f7","lang":"en-US","text":"asks where someone's home is","lesson_id":"8697a61b-9d6d-4265-98c1-565fe58f539e"},{"key":"vocab:9d6ea7a7-7a47-4075-89f2-77b8be14e4f5","lang":"en-US","text":"asks who shares your home (with goes last)","lesson_id":"8697a61b-9d6d-4265-98c1-565fe58f539e"},{"key":"vocab:5c099d00-3387-46fe-baab-f9